# The OpenAPI contract is synced byte-for-byte from the private server repo
# (memforge's scripts/sync-openapi.sh), where it is generated by
# System.Text.Json's indented writer and drift-gated against the server's
# controllers. That writer emits Environment.NewLine: CRLF when generated on
# Windows, LF on Linux CI. Pin this file to LF so a contributor resyncing it
# from a Windows checkout doesn't turn a real one-line contract change into a
# whole-file diff.
spec/openapi.json text eol=lf
